The '''Community Center''' is an [[Location]] found in the {{Zone|Village}} and right behind the [[Hub Island]] spawn. Here, players can participate in the [[Mayor Election]], learn about [[City Projects]], buy [[Fire Sale]]s, and purchase [[Account & Profile Upgrades]] and {{Item|Booster Cookie}}s at {{NPCSprite|Elizabeth}}.

{{ZoneText|Participate in the &aMayor Elections&f.|Contribute to City Projects.|Unlock upgrades, buffs, and cosmetics in the &bCommunity Shop&f.}}

== Purpose ==
=== Mayor Elections ===
{{See also|Mayor Election|Election Room}}

By using the {{Item|Teleport Pad}} at the back of the '''Community Center''', the player can travel to the {{Zone|Election Room}} and vote on one of five Mayors. Each Mayor will have between {{Green|1}}-{{Green|3}} perks, and Mayors with {{Green|3}} perks have a chance to gain a {{Green|4}}th perk; each Mayor will also have a Minister perk, which they will retain if they are the elected Minister. {{NPCSprite|Diaz}}'s {{AN|Long Term Investment}} perk guarantees that the next elected Minister will retain all of their perks.

Every 8 SkyBlock Years, a [[Mayor Election|Special Mayor]] will enter the roster.

On three occasions in SkyBlock history, a special one-time candidate entered the roster: {{NPCSprite|Dante}}, a dictator who was defeated in [[The Uprising]]; {{NPCSprite|Technoblade}}, the [[Resistance Leader]] following the Uprising; and {{NPCSprite|Candidate Aura;Aura}}, a communist who disbanded the mayor elections and introduced the [[Minister Election]], where players could be voted as Minister.

=== Elizabeth ===
{{See also|Elizabeth|Fire Sale}}

{{NPCSprite|Elizabeth}} has several features in the menu, including:

* Viewing [[Fire Sale]]s
* Viewing [[City Projects]]
* Purchasing [[Account & Profile Upgrades]]
* Purchasing items from the [[Bits Shop]]
* Buying {{Item|Booster Cookie}}s
* Purchasing Ranks from the Hypixel Store

While under the effects of a {{Item|Booster Cookie}}, players will be able to obtain {{Bits}}. {{Bits}} can be spent in the [[Bits Shop]] for useful items: most notably, {{Item|God Potion}}s, {{Item|Kismet Feather}}s, [[Enrichments]], [[Abicases]], and other upgrade components.

Fire Sales are events where players can purchase exclusive cosmetics for {{Gems}}, like [[Pet Skins]], [[Helmet Skins]], and [[Barn Skins]].

=== City Projects ===
{{See also|City Projects}}

'''City Projects''' are global projects that all players across SkyBlock are invited to donate their resources to. Upon the completion of the City Project and the completion of the development of its respective update, an update to the game world is pushed.

Contributing to City Projects will grant [[Fame]] and, occasionally, a special bonus related to the project. Contributing enough times will grant a [[Mementos|Memento]].

=== Account Security ===
The '''Community Center''' contains {{NPCSprite|Susan}}, who grants access to the {{Zone|Security Hall}} to players who have reached {{SkyBlock Level|10}} and above. There, players are given a quest from {{NPCSprite|Brigette}} to learn about account security.

